---
import RestaurantLayout from '@personal-sites/reviews/layouts/restaurant';
import type { Restaurant } from '@personal-sites/reviews/restaurants';

export const restaurant: Restaurant = {
  name: 'The Hop Shop',
  suburb: 'Frankston',
  mapsUrl:
    'https://www.google.com/maps/place/The+Hop+Shop/@-38.1448416,145.121712,17z/data=!4m16!1m7!3m6!1s0x6ad675d77461172b:0x6684a37ae68fa3fd!2sThe+Hop+Shop!8m2!3d-38.1448416!4d145.121712!16s%2Fg%2F11k2h2y6fg!3m7!1s0x6ad675d77461172b:0x6684a37ae68fa3fd!8m2!3d-38.1448416!4d145.121712!9m1!1b1!16s%2Fg%2F11k2h2y6fg',
  coordinates: [-38.1448416, 145.121712],
  visited: '2026-09-20',
  dishes: [
    'Pork taco',
    'Fish taco',
    'Beef taco',
    'Chicken taco',
    'Mozzarella sticks',
    'Mushroom taco',
    'Spicy margarita',
    'Negroni',
    'Vodka margarita',
    'Margarita',
    'Street corn',
  ],
};
---

<RestaurantLayout restaurant={restaurant}>
  <div class="visit-notes">
    <p>What a weekend. Broke out the tandem bike, watched/played a shocking amount of footy, made 2 trips to the Erica, finally made it to karaoke, and caught a 6/10 sunset on the beach in beautiful Frankston. The food was terrible, but the company was not, with guest judges Heather and Katelyn joining us.</p>
    <p>Service wasn’t great: messed-up drinks, a weirdly strict ID policy, and gross water. The food and drinks didn’t make up for it. They were out of a bunch of ingredients, Heather’s drink was undrinkable, and the food that arrived was average at best.</p>
    <p>Meg has lost restaurant-picking privileges for the next two outings. We’ll leave her with sunset spot recs. Also, karaoke stage presence needs some more practice.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="shared">
    <h2 id="shared">Shared dishes</h2>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Pork taco</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Meg · 7.2/10</strong></div>
          <p>Spicy as hell! Think they may have put some peppers in this one. Meg was super brave.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Jack · 7.3/10</strong></div>
          <p>Yeah, just alright mate. Technically they were supposed to be al pastor - they were not. Probably a slightly worse version of when I make tacos al pastor. Not a good sign.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="heather" aria-label="Heather’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Heather · 7.4/10</strong></div>
          <p>Don’t think I heard her complain. Great positivity from Heather. Great support for Meg after she ruined everything.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Fish taco</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Meg · 5.2/10</strong></div>
          <p>Tasted less like fish than the last fish taco we tried. Let’s go - almost looked like Meg enjoyed it for half a second. Wow, adventurous, brave Meg.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Jack · 7.4/10</strong></div>
          <p>Not bad. Pretty sure they just refried a fish stick, but the sauce was alright. Again, reminds me of shitty homemade Mexican food.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Beef taco</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Meg · 7.4/10</strong></div>
          <p>Yeah no yeah.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Jack · 7.1/10</strong></div>
          <p>Thought this was going to be the best taco of the night initially, but it was somehow too much meat. They really need to season their meat.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Chicken taco</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Meg · 7.6/10</strong></div>
          <p>Not spicy because they weren’t seasoned. Meg likes this. Think she just likes chicken?</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Jack · 7/10</strong></div>
          <p>Again, why did they not put seasoning on the chicken? Tasted like boiled chicken on an average-at-best tortilla.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Mozzarella sticks</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Meg · 7.7/10</strong></div>
          <p>Cheese.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Jack · 7.9/10</strong></div>
          <p>Don’t know how to feel about these. It wasn’t even the thing we wanted to order, but they tasted alright. Kind of a funky offering.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="heather" aria-label="Heather’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Heather · 7.3/10</strong></div>
          <p>Chucking up a guess here: sorry girl.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="katelyn" aria-label="Katelyn’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Katelyn · 7.6/10</strong></div>
          <p>Likes mozzarella sticks a lot. Unusual batter. Needed another layer of coating to hold everything together.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Street corn</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="heather" aria-label="Heather’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Heather · 0/10</strong></div>
          <p>The worst corn Heather has ever had.</p>
        </section>
        <section data-person="katelyn" aria-label="Katelyn’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>Katelyn · 3/10</strong></div>
          <p>The worst corn Katelyn has ever had.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section solo-reviews" aria-labelledby="meg-extras">
    <h2 id="meg-extras">Meg</h2>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Vodka margarita</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews">
        <section data-person="meg" aria-label="Meg’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>8/10</strong></div>
          <p>A crime against margaritas. Completely unethical, but pretty good. Should have stolen the glass.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section solo-reviews" aria-labelledby="jack-extras">
    <h2 id="jack-extras">Jack</h2>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Margarita</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews">
        <section data-person="jack" aria-label="Jack’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>8.2/10</strong></div>
          <p>Average margarita, but somehow the bright spot of the night. Jack did not bring his ID, which was perfect because they had the strictest ID policy in all of Frankston - will bring a passport next time. Only got it because they messed up someone’s order and just gave us the extra.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section solo-reviews" aria-labelledby="heather-extras">
    <h2 id="heather-extras">Heather</h2>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Negroni</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="heather" aria-label="Heather’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>1/10</strong></div>
          <p>Bartender missed Negroni day at bartending school. Shocking. Possibly the worst attempt at a drink I have seen in my entire time in Australia.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section solo-reviews" aria-labelledby="katelyn-extras">
    <h2 id="katelyn-extras">Katelyn</h2>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Mushroom taco</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="katelyn" aria-label="Katelyn’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>5.8/10</strong></div>
          <p>Good flavour, but dry. How do you make dry mushrooms? They’re like 90% water. The guacamole that was supposed to come with it was missing - that could have helped.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article>
      <div class="menu-line">
        <h3>Spicy margarita</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="reviews guest-reviews">
        <section data-person="katelyn" aria-label="Katelyn’s review">
          <div class="scores"><strong>7.2/10</strong></div>
          <p>The spice was on the rim, not in the drink. Paying extra for just the rim felt a bit much. Katelyn is a bit picky, as we have established in her love life.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</RestaurantLayout>
